  "rationale": "Genome-wide knockout screen (71,090 guides, ~4 per gene, 142 LacZ/luciferase/EGFP control guides) in four KRAS-G12C-mutant NSCLC lines (H2030, H2122, H23, HCC44), each treated with the G12C inhibitor MRTX849 or DMSO for eight doublings in two replicate cultures. Per-sample files merged by guide id (prepare.R); the gene is the guide id's first field. The paper looks for synthetic-lethal dropouts on MRTX across the four lines, so the primary model is ~ cell_line + treatment with MRTX vs DMSO pooled over the lines (8 vs 8, cell line as a paired term; 11 residual df). Synthetic-lethal genes are depleted on MRTX. The T0, TNO155 and MRTX+TNO (COMBO) arms are not in this contrast.",
